# Client Setup

The `Chemical` component sets up the service worker, transports, and core Chemical functions.

## Installation

```svelte
<script>
  import Chemical from "chemicaljs/Chemical";
</script>

<Chemical/>
```

## Using in layout

Add `<Chemical>` to your root layout so it runs across your app, and share its state through `setContext`.

`+layout.svelte`

```svelte
<script>
  import Chemical from "chemicaljs/Chemical";
  import { setContext } from "svelte";

  let { children } = $props();

  let chemState = $state({
    ready: false,
    instance: null,
  });

  setContext("chemState", chemState);
</script>

<Chemical bind:ready={chemState.ready} bind:this={chemState.instance}/>
{@render children()}
```

`+page.svelte`

```svelte
<script>
  import Frame from "chemicaljs/Frame";
  import { getContext } from "svelte";

  let chemState = getContext("chemState");
</script>

<Frame bind:chemical={chemState.instance} bind:ready={chemState.ready} src="https://example.com"/>
```

You can also configure global `plugins` and `adblock` defaults on `<Chemical>` so every `<Frame>` inherits them. See [Plugins](/docs/client/plugins/).
